    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0202" n="162" xml:id="pg162"/>

                <head>24. Letter From the Chairman of the Senate Armed Services Committee (Russell) to the Deputy Assistant Secretary of State
                    for Inter-American Affairs (Snow)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d24-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1959-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1959</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Snow</hi>: Permit me to acknowledge receipt of your
                        letter<anchor n="2" xml:id="d24-f2"/> advising that the rehabilitation and
                    modernization of vessels to be loaned to Latin American countries under Public
                    Law 85–532, will be accomplished by grant aid instead of by loans as the
                    Committee was informed when this legislation was under consideration.</p>
                <p>It occurs to me that the changed economic conditions in Latin America should have
                    been known to the Department of State and to the Department of Navy in 1958.
                    Moreover, I am also of the opinion that the Departments should have anticipated
                    that the Latin American countries might consider that they were being
                    discriminated against when ships were being provided to other countries without
                    charge.</p>
                <p>Although I recognize that the changed financing for the rehabilitation of these
                    vessels is possible under the terms of the authorizing act, I nevertheless
                    desire to register a protest against this departure from the financing indicated
                    in the justification material submitted to the Committee when this authority was
                    under consideration.</p>
                <p>With best wishes, I am</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Richard B.
                        Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
